menu "Find My transport"

    config FIND_MY_TRANSPORT_MODEM_ID
        hex "Public modem identifier"
        default 0x4E555453
        help
            Four-byte public routing identifier (default ASCII "NUTS").
            It is embedded in every candidate public key and is not a secret.
            Configure the receiver with the same hexadecimal value.

    config FIND_MY_TRANSPORT_ADV_INTERVAL_MS
        int "BLE advertising interval (milliseconds)"
        range 20 10240
        default 1000
        help
            Interval between non-connectable BLE advertisements for a symbol.
            ESP32 rounds this value to BLE's 0.625 ms controller units.

    config FIND_MY_TRANSPORT_SYMBOL_DWELL_MS
        int "Dwell time per 2-bit symbol (milliseconds)"
        range 20 60000
        default 1600
        help
            Time each candidate key remains on air. Keep this at least as long
            as the advertising interval so every symbol gets an opportunity to
            be transmitted. Four symbols encode each source byte.

    config FIND_MY_TRANSPORT_HEADER_REPEATS
        int "FMN1 header copies per body pass"
        range 1 32
        default 8
        help
            Number of times the fixed 40-symbol FMN1 header is aired during
            each complete body pass. Copies are distributed across the pass,
            allowing receivers to learn the exact frame length reliably even
            when relay coverage is intermittent.

endmenu
